This software is a plugin for vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, Apache-2.0, Copyright contributors to
the vLLM project). Its GPU kernels are written in Triton (https://github.com/triton-lang/triton, MIT), which is a
dependency and is not included.

This product includes software from vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Copyright contributors to the
vLLM project, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - tritq-qwen36/vllm028_overlay/vllm/ holds seven files of vLLM 0.28.0 (six modified, one new) that add a
    confidence-stop draft depth to Model Runner V2 speculative decoding. They are a port of vLLM pull request
    #60068 ("Confidence stop for autoregressive drafting", by @stecasta, Apache-2.0) as carried by
    salient-data/qwen38-next-dgx-recipe (https://github.com/salient-data/qwen38-next-dgx-recipe), commit f309019,
    recipe/patches/0010-vllm60068-confidence-stop-for-autoregressive-drafting.patch (ported there at PR head 029a811e).
    Each modified file keeps the vLLM SPDX and copyright lines and carries a change notice.
  - tritq-qwen38/patches/0010-vllm60068-confidence-stop-for-autoregressive-drafting.patch is that recipe patch,
    unchanged (its provenance header is kept); the Docker image applies it to vLLM 0.32.0 and keeps it in the image.

