Derived from salient-data/qwen38-next-dgx-recipe (Copyright 2026 Salient Data, Apache-2.0):
  - The skinny-GEMM plan fill in tritq125/vllm_plugin.py (function _patch_skinny_fill, option TRITQ_SKINNY_FILL)
    follows recipe/patches/0011-skinny-gemm-rows.patch ("written for this recipe", commit f309019): the same fill
    rule, applied at run time to every capability table instead of editing vLLM's SM121 table in place.

Reimplemented from a published algorithm (no lines copied):
  - The sparse context-aware draft head (tritq/sparse.py, option TRITQ_DRAFT_HEAD=sparse) reimplements, for the
    packed-trit language-model head, the algorithm of vLLM pull request #59740 ("Context Aware Sparse LM Head", by
    @stecasta, Apache-2.0; also carried by salient-data/qwen38-next-dgx-recipe as patch 0013). Its row-gather kernel
    follows the layout of the PR's gather GEMV kernel.

Ideas credited (no code was copied from these sources; each feature is an independent implementation):
  - Reduced-vocabulary draft head for speculative decoding (TRITQ_DRAFT_HEAD=english): the idea is published in
    FR-Spec (arXiv 2502.14856), VocabTrim (arXiv 2506.22694), community serving recipes for these models, and the
    --mtp-vocab option of the Atlas inference engine (idea only; no Atlas code was copied or adapted; independent
    implementation in Triton).
  - Disk-backed n-gram (PLE) embedding table read through the operating system's page cache: the approach used by
    vLLM's own Qwen3.8 pinned-host n-gram embedding and by community serving recipes (e.g. vllm#54129, vllm#58815).

